# Here Comes the Sun, refrain (figure 183.2)
# Pollack counts mm. 6-7 in eighth notes grouped 3+3+3+3+4 (his asterisks mark the groups); the
# chords and his bassline D C# B A change at the start of the first four groups, which places them
# here: b7/D and A/C# a dotted quarter each, b on beat 3, A on the second eighth of m. 7, E on beat 3.
# He types the chords as "b6/5" and "A6/3" (first-inversion b7 and A, over his D and C#).
# Added: the bass E under the E chord in m. 7 (the chord root; his bassline stops at A).
